## Core SQL Concepts Implemented
* **DDL & DML:** `CREATE DATABASE`, `CREATE TABLE`, `INSERT`, `UPDATE`, `DELETE`
* **Data Retrieval:** `SELECT`, `WHERE`, `ORDER BY`, `GROUP BY`, `HAVING`
* **Relational Joins:** `INNER JOIN`, `LEFT JOIN`, `RIGHT JOIN`
* **Database Objects:** Subqueries, Views, Indexes, Stored Procedures, Triggers, and Transactions

---

## Sample Analytical Queries

### 1. View Active Book Issues (With Joins)
```sql
SELECT m.name, b.title, i.issue_date
FROM Members m
JOIN Issued_Books i ON m.member_id = i.member_id
JOIN Books b ON b.book_id = i.book_id
WHERE i.return_date IS NULL;
```
#### Output

| Name | Book Title | Issue Date |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Ankit Singh | Database Systems | 2025-04-01 |
| Rahul Sharma | Python Programming | 2025-04-03 |

### 2. Identify Most Popular Categories
```sql
SELECT category, COUNT(*) as Total_Issues
FROM Books b
JOIN Issued_Books i ON b.book_id = i.book_id
GROUP BY category;
```

